# C# / .NET (code)

- Prefer idiomatic modern C#; match the repo’s existing style first.
- Keep changes minimal; avoid refactors unless requested.
- Use `async/await` correctly; avoid sync-over-async; include CancellationToken where the repo expects it.
- Prefer dependency injection patterns already present; don’t introduce new DI frameworks.
- Add/adjust tests when behavior changes (per global rule).
